WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:03.040
- [Reporter] If you were
on Chinese social media

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:04.220
at the start of the year

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:06.570
you might have come across this video.

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:08.890
It appears to show a
Tesla Model 3 in flames

00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:11.483
at a Shanghai parking garage.

00:00:11.483 --> 00:00:16.483
(news anchor speaking in foreign language)

00:00:17.177 --> 00:00:19.160
- [Reporter] The reports were
widely watched and shared

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.510
on popular microblogging site Weibo

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:23.860
and messaging app WeChat.

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:25.670
In a statement to Chinese media,

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:27.590
Tesla said that nobody was injured

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:29.370
and the fire was likely caused

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:31.320
by something hitting the bottom of the car

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.980
and damaging the battery
before it caught fire.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.210
Tesla didn't respond to
a request for comment

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:37.910
on the video in question.

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:40.070
Other videos appearing
to show quality issues

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:41.900
in vehicles sold by the EV maker

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:44.270
have surfaced on Chinese social media.

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.680
And after a number of customer complaints,

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:48.910
Tesla was summoned by Chinese regulators

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:50.620
over safety concerns,

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:53.380
casting a shadow over
Tesla's success story

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:55.170
in a country where the Model 3 Sedan

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:57.620
quickly became the
best-selling electric vehicle.

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:01.460
- Tesla has been enjoying
a honeymoon in China,

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:05.090
was viewed with adoring
eyes by people who think

00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:07.650
Tesla is associated with high tech.

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:11.330
But now with this
accumulation of complaints

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:13.850
it's going to be quite a major issue.

00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:16.410
- [Reporter] Quality issues
aren't new for Tesla.

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:18.830
Manufacturing problems
have prompted recalls

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:21.020
and investigations in the US.

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:23.410
In the past, Tesla has swiftly addressed

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:25.180
complaints from customers,

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:28.120
but in the world's largest
electrical vehicle market

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:31.663
these quality issues could
threaten Tesla's meteoric rise.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.930
Tesla has pulled off some major feats

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:37.410
in the last couple years.

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:40.290
Globally, its car deliveries
and market valuation

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:41.750
have grown quickly.

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:45.020
Tesla first entered the
Chinese auto market in 2013

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:47.030
when it opened a showroom in Beijing

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:50.250
and started taking online
pre-orders for its Model S.

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:52.760
- We're incredibly excited to break ground

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:55.120
on the Shanghai Gigafactory.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:56.100
- [Reporter] In 2019,

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:58.750
Tesla became the fourth foreign
car maker in the country

00:01:58.750 --> 00:01:59.920
to run its own plant

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:02.290
without partnering with a Chinese company,

00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:04.470
something local officials
typically require

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:07.270
from foreign companies that
want to operate in the country.

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:10.100
- We want to very much say
thank you and appreciation

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:12.116
for the Shanghai government
and their support.

00:02:12.116 --> 00:02:13.890
- [Reporter] Yunshi Wang is the director

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:15.330
of a group at UC Davis

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:18.210
studying China's
transportation energy sector.

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:19.820
- When Tesla entered China,

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:23.380
US and China were really
in a middle of a trade war,

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:26.880
so there was a huge incentive to showcase

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:29.370
that China is open to the world,

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:33.360
is not discriminating
against foreign investment.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:34.810
- [Reporter] It took
Tesla less than a year

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:37.230
to get its Shanghai plant up and running.

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:38.950
That's half the time it took to launch

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:42.350
its battery-producing
Gigafactory near Reno, Nevada.

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:44.340
After getting funding from Chinese banks

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:46.210
and quick approval from officials,

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:48.620
Tesla was delivering its
first Chinese-made cars

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:51.120
to local drivers by early 2020.

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:54.430
(upbeat music)
(crowd cheering)

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:56.320
And in early 2021,

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:59.380
Tesla started delivering its Model Y cars.

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:00.700
Car sales in China brought in

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:04.930
more than $6.6 billion in
revenue for Tesla in 2020

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:06.390
and helped the car maker reach

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:09.913
a record 500,000 global
vehicle deliveries that year.

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:13.940
But then, in early 2021,

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:16.830
Chinese regulators
reported an unusual uptick

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:19.893
of customer complaints
about Tesla quality issues.

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:22.700
In this online video, for example,

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:24.420
a Tesla driver appears to complain

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:25.770
about the car accelerating

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:27.800
without the driver's foot on the pedal

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:30.160
with cruise control
and autopilot functions

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:31.980
appearing to be turned off.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:34.150
Tesla didn't respond to
a request for comment

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:35.591
on this video.

00:03:35.591 --> 00:03:40.008
(woman speaking in foreign language)

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:45.820
- [Reporter] Authorities say
they held talks with Tesla

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:48.540
on the consumer reported
abnormal acceleration

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:50.180
and battery fires,

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:52.270
warning the car maker
that it needs to abide

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:53.270
by Chinese laws

00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:55.040
and strengthen internal management

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:58.000
to ensure the quality and
safety of its products.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.710
It couldn't be determined whether the cars

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:01.410
in the videos circulating in China

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:03.020
were made in Shanghai.

00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:05.120
The company said it would
investigate the claims

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:06.750
and abide by the law.

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:09.000
It didn't respond to
our request for comment.

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:12.170
Industry observers
question whether the speed

00:04:12.170 --> 00:04:14.430
at which Tesla scaled
up production in China

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:17.160
could have affected the
quality of its cars.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:20.020
- Tesla was meeting a
huge demand in China.

00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:22.420
There was also some rush

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:24.440
that might contribute to the quality

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:28.440
and may not be able to
provide quality products

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:30.400
in time to meet their demand.

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:32.090
- [Reporter] Tesla didn't
respond to our questions

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:33.380
on whether production speed

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:35.700
may have affected quality in China,

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:38.650
but Elon Musk has acknowledged
in a recent interview

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:41.580
that the company has faced
production challenges.

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:43.630
- During that production ramp,

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:47.230
it's super hard to be
in vertical climb mode

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:48.340
and get everything right.

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:49.630
- [Reporter] Industry analysts said

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:52.450
Tesla's response to
regulatory scrutiny in China

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:54.850
differed sharply from the
tone it has usually employed

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:56.830
with regulators in the US.

00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:59.750
In 2018, Musk sparred with US regulators

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:02.890
as they investigated his tweets
about taking Tesla private

00:05:02.890 --> 00:05:05.590
when his company was in a cash crunch.

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:07.570
Tesla never ended up going private.

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:10.190
And in 2020, Musk initially defied

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:12.020
a California County government order

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:14.900
to suspend production due to coronavirus,

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:16.067
and at one point he tweeted,

00:05:16.067 --> 00:05:18.830
"The coronavirus panic is dumb."

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:22.500
Tesla's issues in China right
now aren't necessarily unique.

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:25.070
Other EV makers, including its rival NIO,

00:05:25.070 --> 00:05:27.470
have also reported battery fires.

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:29.210
But transportation analysts say

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:31.320
Tesla needs to protect its reputation

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:34.330
in a market that already
represents 20% of its revenue

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:36.671
and is expected to grow.

00:05:36.671 --> 00:05:39.254
(upbeat music)

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:45.893
- I think Tesla has to be more careful

00:05:45.893 --> 00:05:47.940
than Chinese local companies.

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:51.020
And they're bigger and
they're perceived to be

00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:52.170
a better company.

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:53.540
- [Reporter] Tesla's
been allowed to operate

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:54.650
with relative freedom

00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:56.450
thanks to a loosening of China's rules

00:05:56.450 --> 00:05:59.370
for foreign automakers in 2018.

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:02.880
For instance, many foreign car
makers like GM and Mercedes

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:05.580
were required to partner
with local companies.

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:07.360
But the Silicon Valley company

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:10.090
faces increased competition
from local startups,

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:12.690
including Li Auto and XPeng.

00:06:12.690 --> 00:06:15.320
As it hopes to continue
to gain ground in China,

00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:19.226
pressure from regulators comes
at a critical time for Tesla.

00:06:19.226 --> 00:06:21.809
(gentle music)

